% doublestroke rather than bbm, which has no outline font at all — TeX Live
% ships bbm10.mf and bbm10.tfm but no bbm10.pfb, so lualatex embeds it as a
% Type 3 bitmap. That prints, but the web edition converts the fonts a block
% actually uses into web fonts, and a bitmap is not something it can convert:
% every \onetype came out as an empty box. dsrom10 is Type 1, the glyph is
% the same to the eye, and the PDF stops carrying a bitmap font too.
\usepackage{dsfont}

\newcommand{\onetype}{\mathds 1}
\newcommand{\onelement}{1}

